course: dictionary
lesson: 7777
title: A puzzler: a problem or a person
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words can mean two different things, and puzzler is one of them. A puzzler is a question, problem or mystery that is hard to understand or solve. «That riddle is a real puzzler.» The sentence tells you the riddle is hard, because it is a real puzzler and not an easy one.
explain: A puzzler can also be a person who enjoys doing puzzles, such as crosswords or sudoku. So when you read «good puzzlers try changing each letter position in turn», the word puzzlers means people who love solving puzzles, not the puzzles themselves.
explain: Use the context to choose the right meaning. Ask yourself: is this thing hard to solve, or is this a person who likes puzzles? Then test your meaning in the sentence. Phrases like «a real puzzler» and «a bit of a puzzler» always mean something is hard to work out.
fact: A puzzler is a question, problem or mystery that is hard to understand or solve.
fact: A puzzler can also be a person who enjoys doing puzzles, like crosswords or sudoku.
fact: «A bit of a puzzler» means a little confusing, or hard to work out.
fact: In maths, a puzzler is a tricky problem that needs clever thinking.
fact: «Keen» means eager or very fond of something, so a keen puzzler loves solving puzzles.
exercise: «That riddle is a real puzzler.» What is a puzzler here? | A kind of bird that lives near the sea | *A tricky question or mystery that is hard to solve | A new game for the playground | A quiet, gentle song
exercise: «Mum is a keen puzzler, and she finishes the sudoku every morning.» What does puzzler mean here? | A fast runner | *A person who loves doing puzzles | A loud noise in the kitchen | A broken toy
exercise: Kai is stuck on HEAD to TAIL, changing one letter at a time. For Kai, what is the word ladder? | A song he sings in class | *A puzzler that is hard to finish | A tail on a cat | A duck that swims on the pond
test: What does «a bit of a puzzler» mean? | A very fast car | A small, soft pillow | *A little confusing, or hard to work out | A happy song
test: In «good puzzlers try changing each letter position in turn», what is a puzzler? | A type of letter | A long walk | A loud drum | *A person who enjoys solving puzzles
exam: Which meaning of puzzler is used in «Dad is a keen puzzler, and he never gives up on the crossword»? | A tricky question | A small bird | A loud noise | *A person who loves puzzles
